## 8. Spring Security / `@PreAuthorize`

Authorization is applied **only at the controller method**:

**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** (line 99):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
```

The `@roles` SpEL reference resolves to the Spring bean `Roles`:
**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`**:
```java
@Component
public class Roles {
    public final String OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN";
    public final String VET_ADMIN  = "ROLE_VET_ADMIN";
    public final String ADMIN      = "ROLE_ADMIN";
}
```
So the caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. No `@PreAuthorize`/`@Secured` exists on `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` or the repository.

---

### End-to-end order of operations for `POST /api/owners`
1. Spring Security evaluates `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` → requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (else `AccessDeniedException` → re-thrown by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` → 403).
2. JSON body deserialized to `OwnerFieldsDto`; `OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice.afterBodyRead` runs first (HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE) → any blank required field → 400 `{"errors":[...]}`.
3. `@Valid` bean validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size`) → failure → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 with `schemaValidationErrors`.
4. Controller `addOwner`: `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (ignores `id`, `pets`).
5. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — `@Transactional` → `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (Spring Data JPA persist; entity-level `@NotEmpty`/`@Digits`/`@Pattern` and DB constraints checked at flush/commit; violation → `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404).
6. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`, response `201 Created`.
